# Sibling names, where one spelling begins with the other and neither contains
# it. crates/analyze is not a directory crates/analyzer sits in, so these two
# tasks own nothing in common and both are offered. A prefix test that read
# characters rather than path segments would refuse this pair, and refusing a
# sound queue costs the whole night's work.
run available
exit 0
file tasks/M1-01.md
	---
	id: M1-01
	owns:
	  - crates/analyze
	depends_on: []
	exclusive: no
	---
file tasks/M1-02.md
	---
	id: M1-02
	owns:
	  - crates/analyzer
	depends_on: []
	exclusive: no
	---
stdout
	M1-01
	M1-02
